},"Categories":{"value":"Gracupica contra|Chintamoni Kar Bird Sanctuary|Self-published work|Birds of West Bengal|Files from competitions organized by West Bengal Wikimedians User Group|Files from competitions organized by Wikimedia Bangladesh|Images from Wiki Loves Bangla 2025|Supported by Bangla WikiMoitree|Uploaded via Campaign:Wlbangla","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"This captivating photograph, taken in West Midnapore, West Bengal, beautifully captures two Pied Mynas (Gracupica contra) perched on a bare tree branch against a serene blue sky. These social and vocal birds, recognized by their striking black-and-white plumage with orange beaks and eye patches, are native to the Indian subcontinent. Their melodious calls consist of a mix of whistles, chatters, and mimicry, often heard in pairs or flocks. Interestingly, their scientific name contra has an amusing anecdote in Bengali folklore. It is believed that their constant chatter sounds like a never-ending arguement, as if they are always contradicting each other—hence contra! This composition highlights their natural beauty, with their positioning adding harmony and balance. A perfect representation of West Bengal’s rich biodiversity and cultural connections to nature.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2025-03-21 13:21:52","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<span class=\"int-own-work\" lang=\"en\">Own work</span>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=User:Satyam_Kundu&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"User:Satyam Kundu (page does not exist)\">Satyam Kundu</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 4.0","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Creative Commons Attribution-Share Alike 4.0","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Attributio